# lan-hosts.conf.example -- EXAMPLE for lan-hosts.conf, the single source of
# truth for LAN host addresses. This file is tracked in the repo and ships
# with placeholder values (RFC 5737 TEST-NET-1 / example tailnet addresses).
#
# The REAL, user-owned copy lives at
# "$HOME/Library/Application Support/vpn-switch/config/lan-hosts.conf" and is
# never tracked by git (see .gitignore) or overwritten by the app or install
# scripts once it exists -- see ScriptBundle.swift and
# bin/install-vpn-switch.sh, which create it from this example ONLY if it is
# absent. Edit the App Support copy directly to add/change your real hosts;
# this example is refreshed on every sync/install but your real file is not.
#
# hosts-style: "<name> <lan-ip> <tailnet-ip>" per line, one host per line.
# Comments (#) and blank lines are ignored. Names must be valid DNS labels
# (no dots) -- they are exposed as <name>.home.arpa by the dnsmasq resolver
# (ADR-003) and looked up bare via the home.arpa search domain.
#
# Column 2 (LAN IP): used when Tailscale is down (dns-config-j9y.3 refined
# design) -- this is the address dnsmasq answers for <name>.home.arpa while
# away from the tailnet.
# Column 3 (tailnet IP): used as the FALLBACK tailnet address when Tailscale
# is up but 'tailscale status --json' has no live Peer entry for this host
# (e.g. the peer is offline). When a live peer IS present, lib/lan-dns.sh
# prefers the LIVE address from 'tailscale status --json' over this column,
# since the live address is authoritative and this column can go stale if
# the peer's tailnet IP ever changes. Keep this column populated anyway so
# rendering degrades gracefully when the peer can't be found live.
#
# Read by:
#   - lib/lan-hosts.sh (lan_hosts_lan_ip / lan_hosts_tailnet_ip / lan_hosts_names)
#   - lib/lan-dns.sh (renders the addn-hosts file dnsmasq serves from)
#   - bin/lan-dns-install.sh (generates the dnsmasq config from this file)
#   - bin/dns-verify.sh (Tailscale-off expectations, via lib/lan-hosts.sh)
#
# To add a host: edit your real, user-owned lan-hosts.conf (see path above),
# then re-run bin/lan-dns-install.sh.

streamy 192.0.2.4 100.64.10.4
mac-mini 192.0.2.65 100.64.10.65
